WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.584 --> 00:00:02.002
Hey!

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.669
Hello

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.086
Hi

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:03.545
Hello

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:03.878
Hi

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:04.462
Hi

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:04.963
Hello

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:05.964
Welcome to the

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.007
For All Mankind

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.674
time capsule.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.219
The first season
of For All Mankind

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:13.304
kicks things off in 1969.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.558
With the world watching

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.852
as the first man
lands on the moon.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.439
But it's not Neil Armstrong,

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.607
it's a cosmonaut from
the Soviet Union.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.693
That is the premise of the show.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.237
What would change if the
Soviets landed first.

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:31.948
Spoiler Alert:
EV-ER-Y Thing.

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:34.951
First off, the cold war
only gets hotter

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:36.953
and the Soviets continue
to rock our world

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.204
with yet another first.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.040
Putting the first woman
on the Moon.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.127
So, President Nixon, no
watergate in our show folks,

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:46.880
tells NASA they
have two priorities

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.299
build a base on the
Moon and put a woman on it.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:52.594
That's where all these bad ass
women come into play.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.430
Including yours truly.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.266
America's next
Apollo Astronauts.

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:01.686
My character Margo,

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:03.897
the first woman Flight
Controller at NASA,

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.524
tracks their progress
making sure these women

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:07.484
are up to the task.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.069
You're an Astronaut!

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.529
And for my character Ellen,

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.490
certain things have not
progressed far enough,

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.367
and Ellen still needs
to hide her sexuality

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.496
or risk her career and
this incredible opportunity.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:22.165
Against all odds this
crew of amazing women

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:24.209
knew they had to carry on. . .

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:27.504
and carry on they did with
my character Molly Cobb.

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:28.630
Smile

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.882
Taking her place on Apollo 15

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:31.925
Maybe don't smile.

00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:35.845
and becoming the first
American woman in space.

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:38.515
Which is a milestone moment she

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:41.434
embraces with every
ounce of her typical...

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.436
enthusiasm.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.355
People cheering...

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:46.523
I haven't done anything yet.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.944
Ok. Ok. But she does
discover Lunar Ice.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.531
Which brings humanity one step
closer to living on the Moon.

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:57.867
Houston are you
getting this onscreen?

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:01.329
That discovery leads to the
creation of Jamestown.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.249
The first NASA base on the Moon.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.794
How about that. We're
on the Moon to stay.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.924
Things start to get
crazy when Apollo 23

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:16.761
explodes on the launch pad
stranding Ed, Gordo, and Dani

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:18.888
on Jamestown with
no plan of return.

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:20.682
There's trapped...

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:23.768
And then there's stuck on the
Moon and gonna die trapped.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:27.272
And uh, as a result of this,

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:29.315
Gordo starts losing it big time.

00:02:30.525 --> 00:02:31.609
Hey
-I saw one.

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:34.571
You saw what?
There's an ant in my...
-In your suit.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:35.280
Ahh.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.865
I can feel them.
They're all over me.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:37.365
Calm down.

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:38.908
Ahh, I gotta get
my helmet off.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:39.951
Get it off ahh.
-No.

00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:42.912
If NASA were to find out
about Gordo's antics,

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:44.164
it's over for him.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.999
So, to protect Gordo,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.876
Dani heroically breaks
her own arm.

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:50.461
So Ed can send him
back to Earth with her

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:52.088
and NASA will be
none the wiser.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.007
That's crazy. . .

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.842
You literally
broke your own arm?

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:56.634
Hey!

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.761
A hero's gotta do,
what a hero's gotta do.

00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:02.348
That is true, but
that also means

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.558
Ed is now stuck out on the

00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:05.643
Jamestown Moonbase
completely alone.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.191
Back on Earth.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.818
Margo takes Aleida
Rosales under her wing.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.903
Oh my God

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.571
Congratulations.

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:19.782
As NASA continues to work
towards getting Ed home.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.493
Meanwhile, Ed's wife Karen
is home with Shane,

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:23.369
their young son.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.204
Go to your room!

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.998
Stressed, not knowing
when Ed will return.

00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:29.918
Karen is stretched
thin and distracted.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.045
What's going on?

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.630
Ma'am. I'm afraid
there's been an accident.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.841
Devastated,
(door shuts)

00:03:36.841 --> 00:03:38.218
Karen is forced to make

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:40.720
the most difficult
call of her life.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.263
Karen?

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:43.139
(crying)

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:47.143
Ed spirals, and spirals.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.068
Eventually, Ed snaps out of it

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.279
and he's alerted that
Ellen, aboard Apollo 24,

00:03:58.279 --> 00:04:00.156
is floating past the Moon

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:01.991
without enough fuel to
slow down and land.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.328
Margo, devises a plan
to use the lunar orbit

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:08.081
and sends Ed up into
space to rescue Ellen.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.458
This cannot be
our-our best option.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.669
I'm not gonna stand
here and let you. . .

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.462
This is my call!
I'm in command here —

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:15.463
Capcom, Let's go!

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.756
Yes ma'am.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.009
Ok Ed. Coming up on 15 minutes
left in the window.

00:04:20.009 --> 00:04:21.469
So, now or never.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.100
After a few super
intense minutes.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:32.522
Houston, we have capture.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.486
Margo's plan proves successful

00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:40.196
and Ed returns to the Moon,

00:04:40.196 --> 00:04:41.364
safely, with Ellen.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.866
Our first season ends with Ed

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:45.201
returning to Earth to mourn with

00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:47.578
Karen and Ellen on Jamestown.

00:04:47.578 --> 00:04:50.039
Is there anything you'd like to
say to anyone back home?

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:50.748
Umm.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:53.209
Torn between her
heart and her career.

00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:54.919
I know I don't say it enough,

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:57.463
but I miss you, and I love you

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:58.881
with all my heart. . .

00:04:58.881 --> 00:04:59.716
Larry.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:05.680
Oh wait! Not so fast.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.433
We also launched a huge
rocket out of the ocean.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:13.896
Oh my gosh!

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:14.897
It's massive!

00:05:17.608 --> 00:05:18.609
It's amazing!

